## Installation

:::TuffCodeBlock{lang="bash"}
---
code: |
  pnpm add @talex-touch/tuffex
---
:::

:::TuffCodeBlock{lang="typescript"}
---
code: |
  import { TxChoiceCard } from '@talex-touch/tuffex/choice-card'
  import '@talex-touch/tuffex/choice-card/style.css'
  // It renders TxIcon and TxSkeleton, whose sheets are separate
  import '@talex-touch/tuffex/icon/style.css'
  import '@talex-touch/tuffex/skeleton/style.css'
  import '@talex-touch/tuffex/base.css' // tokens + resets, once per app
---
:::

## Usage

`TxChoiceCard` asks one question and offers the answers as rows: an icon, a label and one line of description. Picking a row emits `select`; the card never moves on by itself.

### Single question

Five rows in one column. The picked row is passed back as `selected`, which tints it and adds a check; the last row is disabled because it needs an account first.

:::TuffDemoWrapper{demo="ChoiceCardSingleDemo" code-lang="vue"}
---
code: |
  <script setup lang="ts">
  import type { ChoiceSelectPayload, ChoiceStep } from '@talex-touch/tuffex/choice-card'
  import { ref } from 'vue'

  const steps: ChoiceStep[] = [{
    id: 'start',
    title: 'Where should we start?',
    options: [
      { id: 'report', label: 'Write a weekly report', description: 'Sum up what shipped and what is next', icon: 'i-carbon-report' },
      { id: 'plan', label: 'Plan tomorrow', description: 'Three priorities, in order', icon: 'i-carbon-calendar' },
      { id: 'inbox', label: 'Catch up on messages', description: 'Everything waiting on a reply', icon: 'i-carbon-email' },
      { id: 'learn', label: 'Learn something new', description: 'A 10-minute primer on any topic', icon: 'i-carbon-education' },
      { id: 'calendar', label: 'Sync my calendar', description: 'Connect a calendar account first', icon: 'i-carbon-calendar-add-alt', disabled: true },
    ],
  }]

  const selected = ref<string>()

  function onSelect({ option }: ChoiceSelectPayload) {
    selected.value = option.id
  }
  </script>

  <template>
    <TxChoiceCard :steps="steps" :selected="selected" @select="onSelect" />
  </template>
---
:::

### Steps

A two-step guide: pick a kind of task, then a concrete one. The second page only exists once the first is answered, and the host moves to it through `v-model:step`. Go back with the arrow and the first answer is still marked; pick another kind and the second page is replaced. `columns="2"` lays the rows out two per row.

:::TuffDemoWrapper{demo="ChoiceCardStepsDemo" code-lang="vue"}
---
code: |
  <script setup lang="ts">
  import type { ChoiceSelectPayload, ChoiceStep } from '@talex-touch/tuffex/choice-card'
  import { computed, ref } from 'vue'

  const step = ref(0)
  const kind = ref<string>()
  const task = ref<string>()

  const kinds: ChoiceStep = {
    id: 'kind',
    title: 'What should we start with?',
    options: [
      { id: 'write', label: 'Write', description: 'Reports, emails, meeting notes', icon: 'i-carbon-pen' },
      { id: 'plan', label: 'Plan', description: 'Schedules, priorities, reviews', icon: 'i-carbon-roadmap' },
      // …learn, organize
    ],
  }

  // The second page follows the first answer: a new kind gives it a new id.
  const steps = computed<ChoiceStep[]>(() => kind.value
    ? [kinds, { id: `tasks-${kind.value}`, title: TITLES[kind.value], options: TASKS[kind.value] }]
    : [kinds])

  // Each page marks its own answer.
  const selected = computed(() => (step.value === 0 ? kind.value : task.value))

  function onSelect({ stepIndex, option }: ChoiceSelectPayload) {
    if (stepIndex === 0) {
      if (kind.value !== option.id)
        task.value = undefined
      kind.value = option.id
      step.value = 1 // the card never advances by itself
    }
    else {
      task.value = option.id
    }
  }
  </script>

  <template>
    <TxChoiceCard
      v-model:step="step"
      :steps="steps"
      :selected="selected"
      :columns="2"
      @select="onSelect"
    />
  </template>
---
:::

### Loading

While the answers load, `loading` swaps the rows for skeleton rows built from the same boxes, so nothing moves when the options arrive. The question stays. Reload runs the round trip again.

:::TuffDemoWrapper{demo="ChoiceCardLoadingDemo" code-lang="vue"}
---
code: |
  <script setup lang="ts">
  import type { ChoiceOption, ChoiceStep } from '@talex-touch/tuffex/choice-card'
  import { useDeferredLoading } from '@talex-touch/tuffex/skeleton'
  import { computed, ref } from 'vue'

  const pending = ref(true)
  const picks = ref<ChoiceOption[]>([])
  // Nothing for 150ms, then at least 400ms: a fast answer never flashes a skeleton.
  const skeleton = useDeferredLoading(pending)

  const steps = computed<ChoiceStep[]>(() => [{ id: 'for-you', title: 'Ready for you', options: picks.value }])

  fetchPicks().then((options) => {
    picks.value = options
    pending.value = false
  })
  </script>

  <template>
    <TxChoiceCard :steps="steps" :loading="skeleton" :loading-rows="3" />
  </template>
---
:::

### Best Practices

- One question per step, three to six answers. Past that, the list stops being something you can take in at a glance.
- Write labels as things the user would say ("Plan tomorrow"), and give the description one line on what happens next.
- Advance in `select`, not in the card: set `v-model:step` when the next question depends on the answer, and stay when it was the last one.
- Give a page a new `id` when its options change with an earlier answer. The new page then blur-fades in, and focus lands on it.
- Pass `selected` for the page on screen, so going back shows what was picked there.
- Bind `loading` through `useDeferredLoading`, and set `loadingRows` to the number of answers coming. A fast answer then never flashes a skeleton, and a slow one does not shift the page when it lands.
- Keep a disabled row rather than hiding it when it needs something first, and say what in its description.
- Pass `prevLabel`, `nextLabel` and `stepLabel` in the page's language. The card ships English defaults and no message catalog.
- Use `columns="2"` where height is short and the card is wide. Below 480px it is one column anyway.
- An icon class only renders if your UnoCSS can generate it. On this site that means the `carbon`, `cib`, `logos` and `twemoji` sets.

## API Reference

### Props

| Prop | Type | Default | Description |
|------|------|---------|-------------|
| `steps` | `ChoiceStep[]` | - | The pages, fields under Types below. Required. With one page there is no pager; with none, nothing renders unless `loading`. |
| `step` | `number` | `undefined` | Current page, 0-based (`v-model:step`). Left out, the card keeps its own page and still emits `update:step`. Clamped to the pages there are. |
| `selected` | `string` | `undefined` | Id of the answer to mark on the page on screen: tinted fill, check, `aria-current`, and the list's Tab stop. |
| `loading` | `boolean` | `false` | Replaces the rows with skeleton rows and sets `aria-busy` on the card. The title and the pager stay. |
| `loadingRows` | `number` | `3` | How many skeleton rows `loading` draws. |
| `columns` | `1 \| 2` | `1` | `2` lays the rows out two per row, left to right. Below a 480px card it falls back to one column. |
| `appear` | `boolean` | `true` | Rows rise in one after another on first render and when `loading` ends. A page change always blur-fades instead. |
| `prevLabel` | `string` | `'Previous'` | Accessible name of the back arrow. |
| `nextLabel` | `string` | `'Next'` | Accessible name of the forward arrow. |
| `stepLabel` | `(current: number, total: number) => string` | `` `${current} / ${total}` `` | Text of the pager counter. Both numbers are 1-based. |

### Events

| Event | Params | Description |
|-------|--------|-------------|
| `select` | `(payload: ChoiceSelectPayload)` | An enabled row was clicked, or activated with Enter or Space. `payload` is `{ step, stepIndex, option }`. The card stays on its page. |
| `update:step` | `(index: number)` | An arrow moved to page `index`, 0-based. |

### Slots

| Slot | Props | Description |
|------|-------|-------------|
| `header` | `{ step: ChoiceStep, stepIndex: number, total: number }` | Replaces the default `<h3>` title, for instance to put an avatar beside the question. Whatever it renders names the card and its answer list, so keep the question in it. |

### Types

`ChoiceStep`, one entry of `steps`:

| Field | Type | Description |
|-------|------|-------------|
| `id` | `string` | Identity of the page. A new id on the page on screen replays the page entrance. Required. |
| `title` | `string` | The question: the card's heading, and the name of its answer list. Required. |
| `options` | `ChoiceOption[]` | The answers. Required. |

`ChoiceOption`, one answer:

| Field | Type | Default | Description |
|-------|------|---------|-------------|
| `id` | `string` | - | Identity within the page, where it must be unique, and what `selected` matches. Required. |
| `label` | `string` | - | The row's title and its accessible name. Required. |
| `description` | `string` | - | One line under the label, announced as the row's description. |
| `icon` | `TxIconSource \| string` | - | A `TxIcon` source, structurally the same as `ITuffIcon`, or an icon class such as `'i-carbon-edit'`, read as `{ type: 'class', value }`. |
| `disabled` | `boolean` | `false` | Shown dimmed; the arrow keys skip it and it emits nothing. |

:::TuffCodeBlock{lang="ts"}
---
code: |
  import type {
    ChoiceCardColumns, // 1 | 2
    ChoiceCardEmits,
    ChoiceCardProps,
    ChoiceOption,
    ChoiceSelectPayload, // { step, stepIndex, option }
    ChoiceStep,
    ChoiceStepLabelFormatter, // (current, total) => string
    TxChoiceCardInstance,
  } from '@talex-touch/tuffex/choice-card'
---
:::

### CSS Variables

| Variable | Description |
|----------|-------------|
| `--tx-choice-card-pad` | Inset between the card edge and the rows. Default `8px`. The card radius grows with it. |
| `--tx-choice-card-option-radius` | Row corner radius. Default `10px`. The card radius is this plus the inset, so the two corners stay concentric. |
| `--tx-choice-card-option-pad-x` | Row horizontal inset, and the title's. Default `12px`. |
| `--tx-choice-card-label-line` | Label line height, and the height of the icon box. Default `20px`. |
| `--tx-choice-card-desc-line` | Description line height. Default `18px`. |

The component reads these and never sets them, so they can be set on the card or on any ancestor. It also writes `--tx-choice-card-index` on each row, the row's place in the entrance stagger.

## Overview

- Markup: a `<section>` named by the question, a header with the pager and the heading, then a `<ul role="list">` of `<li>` rows, each holding a native `<button type="button">`. A button is named by its label (`aria-labelledby`) and described by its description (`aria-describedby`); icons are `aria-hidden`.
- `select` never changes the page. The host advances through `v-model:step`, or stays when the answer was the last one.
- The pager renders only with two or more pages. Each arrow is disabled at its end, and the counter is a `role="status"` region, so a page change is announced.
- Keyboard:
  - the list is one Tab stop (roving tabindex): the selected row, or else the first enabled one; the pager comes before it;
  - Up and Down move to the previous and next enabled row and wrap;
  - in two columns, Up and Down stay in the column, and Left and Right move in reading order;
  - Home and End go to the first and last enabled row;
  - disabled rows are skipped, and keys held with Alt, Ctrl or Meta are left to the page.
- Two columns fall back to one below a 480px card (a container query on the card). The arrow keys read the number of columns actually rendered, so they follow.
- When the page changes while focus is in the list, as when a keyboard pick is answered by advancing, focus moves to the new page's Tab stop. When the arrow in use becomes disabled, focus moves to the other arrow.
- Entrance: on first render, and when `loading` ends, rows rise in 45ms apart (the delay is capped at 360ms); `appear: false` turns this off. A page change blur-fades the heading and the list in together over 160ms. Both are CSS animations on freshly mounted nodes, so rows are clickable from their first frame.
- Under `prefers-reduced-motion: reduce` both entrances are dropped. The resting style is their end frame, so the rows are simply there.
- `loading` draws `loadingRows` skeleton rows in the rows' own boxes (icon box, label line, description line), each with an icon and a description bar. The skeleton is `aria-hidden` and the card `aria-busy`. With no page yet, the title is a skeleton bar too.
- Icons: a string is an icon class, an object goes to `TxIcon` as it is. Once any row on a page has an icon, every row keeps the icon column, so the labels line up.
- The selected row gets the `--tx-color-primary-light-9` fill, a primary ring, a trailing check and `aria-current="true"`, so colour is never the only mark. Its hover deepens the tint.
- Hover changes a row's fill at once; nothing on the card transitions colour. Disabled rows are at 50% opacity with a `not-allowed` cursor.
- With empty `steps` and no `loading`, nothing renders.

## Technologies

- Source: `packages/tuffex/packages/components/src/choice-card/src/TxChoiceCard.vue`, with the types in `src/types.ts`.
- Reference: the "Where do we start?" card of an assistant's opening guide, with icon, title and grey description per answer and a `‹ 1 / 2 ›` pager at the top left. Neighbours that did not cover it: `TxSuggestionChips` has text only and no steps, and `TxRecommendationCard` models one recommendation with a drawer of alternatives.
- The skeleton rows use the loaded row's own containers with `TxSkeleton` bars inside. `--tx-skeleton-base-color` is set to a darker fill (`--tx-fill-color-darker` in the rows, `--tx-fill-color` for the title bar), because the skeleton's own default, the lightest fill, would vanish on the row fill.
- Contrast, measured in all four theme blocks against all four row fills (resting, hover, selected, selected hover), is recorded in the source:
  - the description, in `--tx-text-color-regular`, is at worst 5.06:1 (selected hover, light theme); `--tx-text-color-secondary` was rejected at 2.87:1 on the resting fill;
  - the check is `TxModeChip`'s `info` ink, at worst 4.82:1.
- Rejected designs:
  - `role="listitem"` on the buttons, as `TxSuggestionChips` does, strips their button role; the list uses `<ul>` / `<li>` with the buttons inside;
  - a `<Transition mode="out-in">` for the page change holds the new page back until the old one has left; the list is keyed and animated with CSS instead;
  - an `id` on the `<h3>` would put every demo heading into the docs outline, and would leave a `header` slot unnamed; the id sits on a wrapper.
- Props are declared as a runtime object checked against `ChoiceCardProps`, as in `TxModeChip`: the docs dev server does not recompile an SFC when only its `types.ts` changes.
- **Verified coverage:**
  - `choice-card/__tests__/choice-card.test.ts` covers the markup and names, icons, SSR, the pager (arrow states, `v-model:step` both ways, uncontrolled and controlled pages, clamping, prop strings), selection (payload, no advance, disabled rows, the selected mark), the keyboard (roving tab stop, Up/Down, Home/End, two columns, the rendered column count, focus carried to a new page and to the other arrow), loading and both entrances;
  - `choice-card-motion.test.ts` pins the compiled style: no colour transition anywhere, instant hover fills, animations declared only under `prefers-reduced-motion: no-preference`, start-frame-only keyframes, token-only colour with fallbacks, the row fills, the ring and concentric radii, the type scale, the 480px container query and the focus rings.

